<% content_for(:title) { "CLI & Agents — Dotted" } %>

<main data-page="terminal" data-size="md">
  <section class="terminal-card" aria-labelledby="terminal-heading">
    <div class="terminal-card-bar" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="terminal-card-lights"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span>codex — dotted</span>
      <span>preview</span>
    </div>

    <div class="terminal-card-body">
      <h1 id="terminal-heading">Your journal, from the terminal.</h1>
      <p class="terminal-card-intro">
        Use the Dotted CLI to work with your journal from the terminal, or let
        an agent help you capture and organize what's on your mind.
      </p>

      <div class="terminal-session" aria-label="Illustrative agent session">
        <p><span class="terminal-prompt">$</span> codex</p>
        <p><span class="terminal-prompt">›</span> Add “Review project notes” to Dotted, then show what’s due tomorrow.</p>
        <p class="terminal-response">Added “Review project notes” to your daylog. Tomorrow you have “Send the project update” and “Pick up library books.”</p>
      </div>

      <h2>What you can do</h2>
      <ul class="terminal-capabilities">
        <li>Read and search your bullets</li>
        <li>Create, edit, and complete tasks</li>
        <li>Organize bullets into collections</li>
        <li>Check what’s coming up next</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/spacepolice10/digibujo">View Dotted on GitHub</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
